  "notes": "The layout of Kandy, Lankanatha and Lankapura (FontMonger, \"Copy Right Reserved- LN\"): lower case letters are consonants and vowels, upper case the same consonant with al-lakuna (k = ක, K = ක්). Not the Wijesekara layout: worked out by rendering each glyph and comparing it with Unicode Sinhala; Lankanatha leaves some of these codes empty (P to [, c to k, s to |), the rest match Kandy. Not mapped yet, reported unmapped: the vowel signs ි ී ු ූ, which these fonts only have inside consonant + vowel ligatures on the high code points (0xA1-0xFF), rakaransaya, yansaya and ඟ ඎ.",
